==Battleground==
*5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Ginger Snache]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
**10 [[Ginger Snache]]s (500%) spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Zigge]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**5 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**3 [[Loris|Lorises]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With a bit of luck involving the Sir Seals' spawn times, you can take advantage of the limited number of enemies at the start to stack [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]], or more specifically [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]]. Merely reduce the number of enemies until only one Sir Seal is left and then stall using [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]]. Units that can freeze the Sir Seal without killing him too quickly can also work. However, such units won't be of much use during the boss fight.

The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] are the enemies' primary means of gaining ground, so it would be a good idea to to cancel Zigge's burrow with the [[Cat Cannon]].

